In a world of hyperbole—“Nike is spiraling!” “Lululemon is a mess!”—analyst Simeon Siegel is a proponent of taking the long, and larger, view. 
@sarah_shapiro
 spoke to Siegel about retail’s major players and what’s just around the corner:

$SURF
@surfcashx
 We don’t wait. We choose to deliver to users first. We submitted the app to both Apple and Google weeks ago. Their approval process moves at their own pace, which we cannot control. What we can control is delivering a real, usable experience starting today. Instead of sitting around and waiting, we chose to launch a PWA (Progressive Web App) that works on every browser, on every device. Same features. Same security. And no need to go through App Store gatekeeping. The App Store will approve it when it approves it. But users can pay and use the product right now. ⸻ First Governance Vote: The Market Decides We launched our first governance proposal to decide how fees should be allocated between staking and ecosystem growth. The market chose 30%. That means: •30% of revenue → allocated to staking •70% remaining → allocated to expansion and product development The team is now building the staking platform directly according to these parameters. ⸻ AI + Human Support on Telegram (No waiting, no tickets) We know how bad crypto customer support usually is. You send a DM and have no idea whenor if you’ll get a reply. Especially when your funds are stuck and you’re forced to wait. So we built a new system on Telegram: •AI answers general questions instantly •If you want to talk to a real human → immediately •No tickets •No queues This system will go live officially within 24 hours. Crypto should have better UX, not worse. And support should never be an afterthought. ⸻ What We Shipped •Full transaction history for every payment •Flexible filtering options •Clear visibility into payment status and final settlement time For Non-KYC users in Vietnam, usage is capped at $100 per day. The limit is clearly shown from the start no confusion, no surprises. ⸻ Additional Features Now Live •Login with Google •iPhone 16 users no longer experience Face ID loops •Profile photos are optional sign up and use instantly The system logs every error across the payment flow. If something breaks, the team immediately knows what failed and fixes it fast. Users don’t need to screenshot or explain issues themselves. ⸻ 10 New Countries — Ahead of Schedule Brazil , Mexico , Colombia , Argentina , Nigeria , Zambia , Thailand , Indonesia , the United States , and Canada are coming online. Meanwhile, the Philippines and Vietnam are already live. That brings the total to 12 regions within Q1, even though the original plan was Q2–Q3. ⸻ United States & Canada: Real-World Spending, Every Day The system will support over 40 major brands, including: Starbucks, Walmart, Target, Home Depot, Apple, Nike, IKEA, Tim Hortons, Lululemon. Merchants simply scan a QR code. Users pay with USDC. USDC will be used for everyday spending across four continents. From street food in Vietnam, rent in Brazil, coworking spaces in Mexico, to shopping at Walmart and coffee at Starbucks. No ATM withdrawals. No Telegram escrow groups. No 5–10% fees paid to Visa or Mastercard. ⸻ We Don’t Wait to Create Real Usage Even if some strategic partners move slower than expected, the team continues to build and expand. Network growth does not need to wait for institutional announcements. ⸻ What’s Next •Full PWA rollout within 10–14 days •Native apps continue the review process in parallel •Then another 12 countries will go live with direct payment network integrations •The staking platform is under development based on the 30% parameter chosen by the market •The Telegram support system goes live with this update •Governance happens through the market, driven by participants with real skin in the game •Country managers operate on the ground, building real local partnerships •Real payments are already happening at meetups and in cafés This is not a roadmap on slides. This is what’s being used right now.

